  "raw_response": "{\n  \"title\": \"Double Zone Breakout with Pullback and Liquidity Sweep: Price breaks two demand zones, forms double top, then sweeps upper liquidity before downside continuation\",\n  \"school\": \"Smart Money Concepts (SMC)\",\n  \"asset\": null,\n  \"timeframe\": \"15m\",\n  \"market_context\": \"Price had broken two successive demand zones in a bearish single-leg move, creating a new supply zone at the extreme. After a pullback, it formed a double top (equal highs) above a decisional supply zone, indicating unresolved liquidity above.\",\n  \"key_observation\": \"The analyst emphasized that traders must wait for a liquidity sweep of the upper supply zone (above the double tops) before entering short trades, as entering at the decisional zone risks being stopped out by the sweep.\",\n  \"analysis_steps\": [\n    \"Step 1: Identify that price broke two successive demand zones in a bearish single-leg move, forming a new HTF supply zone at the extreme.\",\n    \"Step 2: Observe the subsequent pullback that failed to mitigate the extreme supply zone and instead formed a double top (equal highs) with liquidity pools marked by '$' symbols.\",\n    \"Step 3: Recognize the lower supply zone as the 'decisional zone' and the upper one as the 'extreme zone', warning against entering at the decisional zone.\",\n    \"Step 4: Conclude that price is likely to sweep the upper liquidity (above double tops) to trigger stop-losses before continuing downward, making the sweep a required confirmation for short entries.\"\n  ],\n  \"outc",
